&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Code
&lt;/h2&gt;


&lt;div class="ltag-github-readme-tag"&gt;
&lt;div class="readme-overview"&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;
&lt;img src="https://assets.dev.to/assets/github-logo-5a155e1f9a670af7944dd5e12375bc76ed542ea80224905ecaf878b9157cdefc.svg" alt="GitHub logo"&gt;
&lt;a href="https://github.com/Demo-For-Test" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;
Demo-For-Test
&lt;/a&gt; / &lt;a href="https://github.com/Demo-For-Test/ecosloth-ai" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;
ecosloth-ai
&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;
EcoSloth AI - Local AI-Powered E-Waste Assistant for Hacktoberfest 2026 (Week 3: Slow and Steady)
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="ltag-github-body"&gt;

&lt;div id="readme" class="md"&gt;&lt;div class="markdown-heading"&gt;
&lt;h1 class="heading-element"&gt;🦥 EcoSloth AI — Local AI-Powered E-Waste Assistant&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;“Don't throw it away. Let AI find its next life.”&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/Demo-For-Test/ecosloth-ai/LICENSE" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/784362b26e4b3546254f1893e778ba64616e362bd6ac791991d2c9e880a3a64e/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f4c6963656e73652d4d49542d677265656e2e737667" alt="License: MIT"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;a href="https://www.python.org/" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/13466c63b4f964f1bc47e46eabb6ea9ebff2cb7777cba82af790a55719bbbfda/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f707974686f6e2d332e31302532422d626c75652e737667" alt="Python 3.10+"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;a href="https://ollama.ai" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/6b641a22829ffd9cb6934e049ac4b039fce2e28618a41a61dcb3478e0d237b6e/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f4f6c6c616d612d4f66666c696e6525323046697273742d6f72616e67652e737667" alt="Local AI: Ollama"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;a href="https://streamlit.io" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/141ad0c5f024326bc83fd7f27af1a60ab897bf570e85b864f9d6ecc82cfa495d/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f55492d53747265616d6c69742d7265642e737667" alt="Streamlit UI"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;a href="https://pytest.org" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/4935fa3ed1a3c6e8df17e55fd8a1b8c8d5cb52f5c9e8b348c31205b2cab8b740/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f74657374732d7079746573742d737563636573732e737667" alt="Tests: Pytest"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;EcoSloth AI is a local-first, privacy-preserving AI assistant built for the &lt;strong&gt;DEV Open-Source AI Challenge (Hacktoberfest 2026, Week 3: “Slow and Steady”)&lt;/strong&gt;. It helps individuals and organizations evaluate discarded or aging electronic devices to find the most responsible and circular next-life pathway: &lt;strong&gt;Repair, Reuse, Donate, Resell, or Responsibly Recycle&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="markdown-heading"&gt;
&lt;h2 class="heading-element"&gt;🌟 Motivation &amp;amp; Problem Addressed&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Electronic waste (e-waste) is the world's fastest-growing municipal waste stream. When electronics are discarded prematurely:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Embodied Energy is Lost:&lt;/strong&gt; Up to 80% of a computer's total lifetime carbon footprint occurs during manufacturing and rare-earth extraction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Toxic Chemicals Leach:&lt;/strong&gt; Heavy metals (lead, cadmium, mercury) pollute soil and water if landfilled.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Batteries Cause Fires:&lt;/strong&gt; Crushed lithium-ion batteries are a leading cause of fires in municipal recycling trucks and waste sorting facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Most people discard devices simply because researching…&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="gh-btn-container"&gt;&lt;a class="gh-btn" href="https://github.com/Demo-For-Test/ecosloth-ai" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;View on GitHub&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;p&gt;The repository is modular and open-source under the MIT license:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;app.py&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Streamlit multi-page interface with real-time model switching and local SQLite dashboard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;services/safety_rules.py&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Deterministic hazard engine guaranteeing safety boundaries regardless of LLM temperature.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;services/device_assessor.py&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Category classifier and question generator.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;services/recommendation_engine.py&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Circular triage logic mapping devices to repair, reuse, donation, resale, or recycling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;services/checklist_generator.py&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Non-destructive preparation instructions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;services/image_analyzer.py&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Multimodal vision inspection with local models and anti-hallucination disclaimers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;services/history_store.py&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Local SQLite persistence for device outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;services/export_service.py&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Generates Markdown, TXT, and printable HTML reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;tests/&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: 14 automated unit tests verifying model disconnections, malformed JSON, and safety overrides.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How I Built It
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;EcoSloth AI is built around a local-first, open-weight AI architecture:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Local Inference Engine:&lt;/strong&gt; Powered by &lt;a href="https://ollama.ai" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Ollama&lt;/a&gt;, running open-weight models on &lt;code&gt;localhost:11434&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Primary Text Models:&lt;/strong&gt; 

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;llama3.2:3b&lt;/code&gt; (Meta Llama 3.2 Community License) &amp;amp; &lt;code&gt;qwen2.5:3b&lt;/code&gt; (Apache 2.0) for fast, structured JSON generation and device triage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;llama3.2:1b&lt;/code&gt; for ultra-low resource devices (runs on 2 GB RAM).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Multimodal Vision:&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;llama3.2-vision:11b&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;llava:7b&lt;/code&gt; for local physical device and damage inspection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Structured Validation:&lt;/strong&gt; Pydantic v2 schemas (&lt;code&gt;DeviceInput&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;RecommendationOutput&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;DeviceAssessmentResult&lt;/code&gt;) ensuring reliable, strictly validated JSON schemas from model outputs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Deterministic Hybrid Safety Layer:&lt;/strong&gt; LLMs are paired with deterministic rule engines. If a user describes a swollen pouch cell or a high-voltage cathode-ray tube, immutable code overrides the prompt to enforce physical containment before calling the model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Offline Fallback Architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; If Ollama is offline or uninstalled, the system seamlessly transitions to a built-in deterministic heuristic engine. The app never crashes when offline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Why Does Open Innovation Matter?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Open innovation is what made EcoSloth AI possible:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hardware &amp;amp; Personal Data Privacy:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
E-waste triage involves serial numbers, device specs, accounts, and photos of private home spaces. Sending this telemetry to closed commercial cloud APIs (like OpenAI or Anthropic) introduces ongoing SaaS subscription fees and privacy exposure. Open weights allow users to triage tech completely offline on their own hardware with &lt;strong&gt;zero data egress&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Perpetual Software Longevity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Closed APIs suffer from deprecation schedules, price hikes, and sudden endpoint shutdowns. An e-waste tool that stops working because a commercial vendor changed their API pricing defeats the purpose of sustainability. Open weights downloaded via Ollama will run in 10 years exactly as they do today.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsible AI Transparency:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Commercial black-box models often claim they can "see everything." With open-source models, we can inspect model weights, verify licenses (Apache 2.0 / Llama Community), benchmark exact capabilities, and candidly document that ordinary cameras cannot detect internal battery degradation behind aluminum casings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


My Agent Session
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This application was engineered with pair programming assistance from an autonomous AI coding agent. The agent handled:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architecture scaffolding and Pydantic schema validation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing deterministic regex-backed safety firewalls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Writing a comprehensive pytest test suite with mocked Ollama API responses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Crafting clean Streamlit UI components and multi-format export engines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The Lazy Payoff
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Before EcoSloth AI:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
You find an old 2018 iPad or a 2017 ThinkPad in a closet. To do the right thing, you had to:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Google whether the battery is still safe: 10 mins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Search Apple/Lenovo forums for how to remove activation locks and wipe data without bricking the device: 15 mins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Browse Reddit for repurposing ideas (can it run Linux or act as a smart home monitor?): 15 mins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Search municipal sites for real e-waste drop-offs that don't charge hidden fees: 10 mins.
&lt;em&gt;Total effort: ~50 minutes of friction. Result: Most people give up and leave it in the drawer or throw it in the trash.&lt;/em&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;With EcoSloth AI:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pick device category and condition (30 seconds).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Click "Generate Next-Life Action Plan" (2 seconds).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow the interactive checklist (decouple accounts, factory reset, apply thermal tape).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Export the Markdown plan or print a physical handoff label.
&lt;em&gt;Total effort: 2 minutes. The laziness hurdle is completely gone, and another device stays out of the landfill.&lt;/em&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Prize Categories
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Primary Track:&lt;/strong&gt; Hacktoberfest Open-Source AI Challenge — Week 3: &lt;em&gt;“Slow and Steady”&lt;/em&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This file has also been saved to &lt;a&gt;&lt;code&gt;docs/hacktoberfest_article.md&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and pushed to your GitHub repository.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Disclosure: I'm the founder of Jobspiq, which is one of the tools below. Every other product is described from its own public pages as read in October 2026. I didn't test other services' alert speed and make no claim about it. The full comparison, with a link to every source, is on &lt;a href="https://jobspiq.in/blog/job-alert-apps-for-developers-india-2026" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;jobspiq.in&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quick answer:&lt;/strong&gt; use one large portal for reach (LinkedIn or Naukri) and one fast alert service for the companies you care about. Which fast service suits you depends on where it looks for jobs and how it reaches you: email, app push or Telegram.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


At a glance
&lt;/h2&gt;

