Summarize on this device
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;busy&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"button"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;cancel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Cancel&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"status"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;view&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;phase&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;preparing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Preparing on-device summarization…&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;view&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;phase&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;downloading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`Downloading model: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;view&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;percent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;%`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;view&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;phase&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;summarizing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Summarizing…&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;view&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;phase&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;cancelled&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Summary cancelled.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;view&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;phase&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;done&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Summary ready.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;view&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;phase&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;view&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;view&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;phase&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;done&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Summary of this brief&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;style&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;whiteSpace&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;pre-wrap&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;view&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Generated on this device. Check details against the original brief.&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;section&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Place the readiness explanation and a readiness-retry button beside this control in the parent. A disabled action should have a reason the person can read.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Render the plain-text result through React text interpolation. The summary does not need HTML insertion.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Long inputs can exceed the model’s input quota. The &lt;a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Summarizer/summarize" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;code&gt;summarize()&lt;/code&gt; API&lt;/a&gt; can reject with &lt;code&gt;QuotaExceededError&lt;/code&gt;; the hook turns that into a request to choose a smaller section. For a document-oriented feature, &lt;code&gt;measureInputUsage()&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;inputQuota&lt;/code&gt; can support an earlier check. A character count is not an exact token or quota measurement.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The fallback remains useful: the person can read and edit the original brief, then use the rest of the form. A cloud summary could be a separate action with a clear explanation that it sends the text to a server. Failure of the local path should not silently trigger that transfer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Test lifecycle behavior and summary quality separately
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The existing &lt;a href="https://github.com/rajudandigam/trip-workbench/blob/4b3f37034fc291ad5221969e0507d349878dc150/tests/unit/summarizer.test.ts" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Summarizer unit test&lt;/a&gt; checks the missing-API case. That is a useful start, but it does not establish behavior during downloads, cancellation, or editing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For the adapter shown here, eight controlled checks pass with a fake Summarizer. They cover availability states, availability errors, cancellation before creation, immediate creation in the call path, cancellation during creation, progress and input forwarding, rejected late output, and cleanup after generation errors.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These are lifecycle results. The React wiring has not been mounted in a browser during this walkthrough, and no native model output or performance measurement is claimed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use component tests for replacement requests, brief changes, draft changes, unmounting, and Strict Mode cleanup. Assert that an old result never appears beside a new source. Keep those tests deterministic with deferred promises.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Then run native browser checks with a small set of briefs:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Case&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What to inspect&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;First use on a supported device&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Readiness, download feedback, cancellation, and eventual completion&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Model already ready&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Creation and generation latency without mixing in first-download time&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Brief edited during generation&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Old output disappears and cannot return&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Unsupported configuration&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A clear explanation and an intact editing workflow&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Long brief&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A recoverable quota response with the original text retained&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Travel brief above&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Dates, negation, conditions, and uncertainty preserved without invented commitments&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For the travel brief, record whether the output preserves “do not book a hotel,” the client-confirmation condition, and the uncertain return date. These are evaluation criteria, not recorded model results.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Measure correctness alongside usefulness: how long it takes the person to review the summary and source, how often important details are omitted, and whether the summary saves effort at all. Very short briefs may be faster to read directly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This gives the feature a clear role in the wider assistant: a local reading aid, tied to one version of the source, that leaves the original available for human review and the later Gemini proposal.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Hey everyone 👋&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Last time I shared my rebuilt portfolio with a terminal theme. It has a third theme now (a notebook one), and I built a small &lt;strong&gt;playground&lt;/strong&gt; just to switch between them 😄&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Meet &lt;strong&gt;Theme Studio&lt;/strong&gt; → &lt;a href="https://mahmad.me/theme-studio" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;mahmad.me/theme-studio&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F4xsz6htmd3d64kz6ef6h.gif" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F4xsz6htmd3d64kz6ef6h.gif" alt="Dragging a wire into the display" width="720" height="405"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How it works
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The three versions of my site are cards on a canvas, with a display in the middle. To open one, you &lt;strong&gt;drag a wire&lt;/strong&gt; from its card into the display, like plugging a cable into an old TV. 🔌&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The fun parts
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;⚡ &lt;strong&gt;Lightning sparks&lt;/strong&gt; jump between the wire and the display when you get close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;strong&gt;Skill icons&lt;/strong&gt; ride down the wire once it's plugged in.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📺 The &lt;strong&gt;screen turns on like an old TV&lt;/strong&gt;, and then the page opens.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Fast navigation from every page
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I didn't want people to hunt for the playground, so a small live copy of it sits in the bottom-right corner of the home page, the terminal theme and the notebook theme (on desktop). It plugs in one theme after another, and one click opens the real thing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F8crs2l2g056kpbyszivr.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F8crs2l2g056kpbyszivr.png" alt="The corner card on the notebook theme" width="800" height="500"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

