&lt;br&gt;


&lt;p&gt;If you like it, a star ⭐ really helps. What should I plug into the display next? Tell me in the comments 👇&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React is a JavaScript library used to build interactive user interfaces, especially for websites and web applications.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React helps you build websites using reusable pieces called components.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Install React&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
The easiest way to start a new React project is with Vite.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Open your terminal and run:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npm create vite@latest my-react-app
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;cd &lt;/span&gt;my-react-app
npm &lt;span class="nb"&gt;install
&lt;/span&gt;npm run dev
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Choose React → JavaScript when prompted. Then open the local URL displayed in your terminal, usually &lt;a href="http://localhost:5173/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;http://localhost:5173/&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2.Your first React component&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Create or replace the code in src/App.jsx:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;App&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Hello, Sajin Joe!&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Welcome to React.&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;App&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Explanation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;function App() creates a component.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;return describes what appears on the screen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JSX lets you write HTML-like markup inside JavaScript.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;export default App allows another file to import the component.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;React component names normally start with a capital letter.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TL;DR:&lt;/strong&gt; Babelize parses every file with a Babel AST, extracts only user-facing text (whole JSX sentences become ICU messages with placeholders, tags and plurals), names keys from the file path and first words, hashes source text into a lockfile so reruns only translate what changed, validates every LLM translation for lost placeholders, broken ICU and untranslated output, then rewrites components to use next-intl and opens a diff or pull request for review.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Every React app starts with hardcoded text, and nobody wants to spend a sprint moving 900 strings into JSON files by hand. This is how Babelize does it: an AST pass that finds the text worth translating, keys that stay stable between runs, a lockfile so reruns cost nothing, an LLM whose output we refuse to trust, and a code rewrite that keeps your formatting. Plus the cases where it deliberately stops and asks you.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The Problem: Text Lives Inside Components
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A typical Next.js page looks like this:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/app/dashboard/page.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Dashboard&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Welcome back, &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Read the &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Link&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;href&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"/terms"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;terms&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Link&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; before you continue.&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;placeholder&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"Search projects"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"input"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; projects&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Find-and-replace can't localize this. "Welcome back," and &lt;code&gt;{user.name}&lt;/code&gt; are one sentence, and other languages put the name somewhere else. The link sits in the middle of a sentence. &lt;code&gt;placeholder&lt;/code&gt; is user-facing, &lt;code&gt;className&lt;/code&gt; isn't. "projects" needs a plural form, and Polish has four of them. Doing it properly means understanding the code, not the text.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 1: Find the Strings with an AST, Not a Regex
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every file is parsed with &lt;code&gt;@babel/parser&lt;/code&gt; (JSX and TypeScript plugins, with error recovery so one broken file doesn't stop the run). Then visitors walk the tree looking for JSX text, whole JSX elements, string literals, template literals, &lt;code&gt;+&lt;/code&gt; concatenations and both branches of ternaries.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Most of the work is deciding what &lt;em&gt;not&lt;/em&gt; to extract:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Attributes:&lt;/strong&gt; only an allowlist is user-facing: &lt;code&gt;title&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;placeholder&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;alt&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;aria-label&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;aria-description&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;label&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;description&lt;/code&gt; (plus &lt;code&gt;accessibilityLabel&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;accessibilityHint&lt;/code&gt; for React Native). &lt;code&gt;className&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;href&lt;/code&gt; and everything else is left alone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Objects:&lt;/strong&gt; a string under a copy-like key (&lt;code&gt;label&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;title&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;message&lt;/code&gt;) is UI text; under a data-like key (&lt;code&gt;href&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;url&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;className&lt;/code&gt;) it's data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Calls:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;console.*&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;throw&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;new Error(...)&lt;/code&gt; and hook arguments are skipped, along with almost every other call argument.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Values that look like data:&lt;/strong&gt; URLs and paths, CSS selectors, colors, ISO dates, all-caps identifiers like &lt;code&gt;SKU12345&lt;/code&gt;, pure numbers and symbols, and text under three characters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Files:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;node_modules&lt;/code&gt;, build output, tests, specs and &lt;code&gt;.d.ts&lt;/code&gt; files.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Sentences, not fragments
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The key decision: a JSX element with mixed children becomes &lt;strong&gt;one ICU message&lt;/strong&gt;, so translators see the whole sentence. Interpolations become named placeholders, and inline tags like &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Link&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;b&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;code&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; become tags inside the message:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;"Welcome back, {name}"
"Read the &amp;lt;link&amp;gt;terms&amp;lt;/link&amp;gt; before you continue."
"{count, plural, one {# project} other {# projects}}"
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The plural comes from a deliberately narrow rule: exactly one placeholder with a count-like name (&lt;code&gt;count&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;total&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;n&lt;/code&gt;, or ending in &lt;code&gt;Count&lt;/code&gt;), referenced directly, and followed by an English noun we can singularize. &lt;code&gt;{data?.count} items&lt;/code&gt; doesn't qualify, because if &lt;code&gt;data&lt;/code&gt; is undefined you'd ship "NaN items" in nine languages.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When an element can't be folded into a sentence safely (a child expression with side effects, spread props, children passed through, literal braces in the text), it's kept as separate fragments and you get a warning instead of a guess.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 2: Keys That Stay Put
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Key names are boring on purpose. The namespace comes from the file path, with noise like &lt;code&gt;src&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;app&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;components&lt;/code&gt; and a trailing &lt;code&gt;page&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;index&lt;/code&gt; stripped. The key is the first five words, camelCased. So "Welcome back, {name}" in &lt;code&gt;src/app/dashboard/page.tsx&lt;/code&gt; becomes &lt;code&gt;dashboard.welcomeBack&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Collisions get &lt;code&gt;_2&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;_3&lt;/code&gt; suffixes. On later runs, a string whose text hasn't changed gets its existing key back instead of a new copy, so a rerun never renames keys under you.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 3: A Lockfile, So Reruns Are Nearly Free
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Localization isn't a one-off, because you keep shipping English. So every key's source text is hashed (SHA-256) into a lockfile, along with its translations per locale:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;.babelize/local/babelize-lock.json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;On the next run, keys fall into four groups:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Unchanged:&lt;/strong&gt; reused, nothing sent anywhere.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;New:&lt;/strong&gt; translated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Changed source:&lt;/strong&gt; the hash differs, so it's translated again.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Missing a locale:&lt;/strong&gt; you added Japanese, or the glossary changed, so only the gaps are translated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Commit the lockfile with your code. Teammates and CI then get the same "already translated" view, and a rerun after a small feature only pays for the handful of strings you added.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 4: Translate, Then Don't Trust the Output
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Keys go to the model in batches of 15, three batches at a time. You can use your own key (Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini, Groq, OpenRouter) or Babelize's hosted translation. Before sending, placeholders, tags and brand names are swapped for opaque tokens like &lt;code&gt;[#VAR_0#]&lt;/code&gt;, and the prompt says each must come back exactly once. ICU messages keep their argument names, &lt;code&gt;#&lt;/code&gt;, and the target language's own plural categories.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Then every value is checked before it's written:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Placeholder lost:&lt;/strong&gt; a token is missing or duplicated, so &lt;code&gt;{name}&lt;/code&gt; would never render.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Invalid ICU:&lt;/strong&gt; the plural or select no longer parses, or a branch was dropped.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Markup mismatch:&lt;/strong&gt; the &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;link&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; tag disappeared from a branch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Untranslated:&lt;/strong&gt; the model handed the English back.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A rejected key gets one targeted repair attempt, with a note telling the model what was wrong. If that fails too, the key is &lt;strong&gt;left out of the locale file&lt;/strong&gt;. It's never filled with English and never shipped broken. It's also kept out of the lockfile, so the next run retries it, and the CLI exits with code 6 so CI notices a partial run.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 5: Rewrite the Code Without Wrecking Your Diff
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Injection reuses the exact source positions recorded during extraction, and rewrites files with recast, so your formatting, comments and quote style survive. For Next.js App Router projects with next-intl:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A component that's already &lt;code&gt;async&lt;/code&gt; and isn't in a &lt;code&gt;'use client'&lt;/code&gt; file gets &lt;code&gt;await getTranslations()&lt;/code&gt;. Everything else gets &lt;code&gt;useTranslations()&lt;/code&gt;. Components are never made async behind your back.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rich text becomes &lt;code&gt;t.rich()&lt;/code&gt; with your original element passed back in, so the link keeps its &lt;code&gt;href&lt;/code&gt; and props.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useTranslations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;dashboard.welcomeBack&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;rich&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;dashboard.readTheTermsBeforeYou&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;link&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;chunks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Link&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;href&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"/terms"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;chunks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Link&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Then the project is wired up:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;i18n/request.ts&lt;/code&gt; picks the language from a &lt;code&gt;NEXT_LOCALE&lt;/code&gt; cookie, then the browser's &lt;code&gt;Accept-Language&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;next.config&lt;/code&gt; is wrapped with next-intl's plugin, and the root layout's children with &lt;code&gt;NextIntlClientProvider&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Messages go to &lt;code&gt;public/locales/&amp;lt;locale&amp;gt;.json&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;No middleware and no &lt;code&gt;/de/...&lt;/code&gt; routes, so your URLs, auth and redirects stay untouched.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On local runs, your own Prettier or Biome config then runs on the changed source files, so the diff reads like a teammate wrote it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What It Refuses to Guess
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The interesting part of a tool like this is where it stops. Babelize reports these instead of improvising:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Module-level constants&lt;/strong&gt; used outside a render: translating them at import time would freeze one language. You get "move it inside the component".&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Strings with no place for a hook&lt;/strong&gt;, outside any component: extracted and translated, but listed as not wired in, with the reason.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Dynamic keys&lt;/strong&gt; like &lt;code&gt;t(`status.${s}`)&lt;/code&gt;: once one appears, the "unused keys" report turns itself off rather than flagging keys that are in use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;A run that would delete existing translations&lt;/strong&gt; aborts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Hardcoded dates and currency&lt;/strong&gt; get a warning, because formatting them belongs to &lt;code&gt;Intl&lt;/code&gt;, not to translators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Local Diff or Pull Request
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There are two ways to run the same pipeline:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npx babelize
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This runs in your project folder. It needs a git repo and a clean working tree, works on a temporary copy of the project, and only writes back if none of your files changed in the meantime. You review with &lt;code&gt;git diff&lt;/code&gt; and commit, lockfile included. With your own LLM key in the environment you don't need an account.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Or connect the repo with the GitHub App. The same pipeline then opens a pull request, and can keep one PR per branch up to date as you push.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Either way the rule is the same: nothing lands in your code until a human reviews it. Localization tools that write straight to production are how you end up with "Willkommen zurück, undefined".&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Written with AI assistance and reviewed by the Babelize team. Every technical detail was checked against the Babelize engine source.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published on the &lt;a href="https://www.babelize.co/blogs/how-babelize-localizes-nextjs-app/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Babelize blog&lt;/a&gt;. Disclosure: Babelize is our product, an AI localization tool for Next.js, React and Vue apps: it turns hardcoded strings into a reviewed i18n pull request.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


TL;DR
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Pick v0 when you need a screen you can click through before a repository exists: it writes Next.js, Tailwind CSS and shadcn/ui code in a hosted sandbox, previews it and deploys to Vercel. Pick Claude Code when the screens belong in a repository you already have, next to your components, rules and tests. You own the code either way, entry plans cost $20 to $30 a month, and many screens stay consistent when each one imports the same component files, which v0 sets up with Design Systems 2.0 and Claude Code with a registry and a rules file.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The v0 vs Claude Code question usually gets answered on one component: a card or a form, generated in a minute. The harder part starts at the third screen. A sign-in page, a pricing page and a settings page belong to one product, so they have to share buttons, fields, spacing and tone, call your real API, and still match after six months of changes. This post compares v0 and Claude Code on that yardstick: who owns and maintains the code, how each keeps many screens consistent, what each costs and where each one wins. Lovable sits alongside.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We build Wingo UI, a component registry that Claude Code installs from, so read this as a vendor's view. We ran no generation benchmark and show no v0 or Lovable output: what we say about them comes from their docs and pricing pages, checked in October 2026 and linked. The Claude Code side uses our real Login, Pricing and Settings Page blocks. More head to head posts live under &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/category/comparisons" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Comparisons and alternatives&lt;/a&gt;, and the &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/shadcn-alternatives" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;shadcn alternatives guide&lt;/a&gt; covers the libraries these tools install.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How are v0 and Claude Code different?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;v0 is a hosted builder: you chat on v0.app, it writes code in a sandbox, previews it and deploys to Vercel. Claude Code is an agent in your repository: it reads and edits your files, runs your commands and commits through git, from the terminal, an IDE, the desktop app or the web. Lovable is another hosted builder with a live preview, and it picks the framework and the database for you.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As of October 2026, from each vendor's own docs:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;v0&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Claude Code&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Lovable&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Where the work happens&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A Vercel Sandbox virtual machine, with a live preview&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Your machine or a cloud session, inside your repository&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Lovable's hosted editor, with a live preview&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Stack it writes&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Next.js, React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Whatever your repository uses&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;TanStack Start for new apps, React with Vite for older ones; no framework choice&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Existing repository&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Import from GitHub, a Vercel project or a ZIP&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Starts there&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Cannot connect an existing repository&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;How code leaves&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;GitHub sync: a branch per chat, then a pull request&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Already in your repository; commits and pull requests through git&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Git sync on every plan, ZIP download on paid plans&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Teaching it your design system&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Design Systems 2.0, saved as a skill&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;CLAUDE.md&lt;/code&gt;, skills, MCP servers and the component files themselves&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Design systems on paid plans, copied into each connected project&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Entry paid plan&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Plus, $30 per user per month&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Claude Pro, $20 a month&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Pro, $25 a month for 100 credits&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Sources: the v0 &lt;a href="https://v0.app/docs/faqs" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;FAQ&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://v0.app/docs/github" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;GitHub docs&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://v0.app/docs/design-systems-2" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Design Systems 2.0&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://v0.app/pricing" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;pricing&lt;/a&gt;; the Claude Code &lt;a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/overview" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;overview&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://claude.com/pricing" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Claude pricing&lt;/a&gt;; the Lovable &lt;a href="https://docs.lovable.dev/introduction/faq" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;FAQ&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://docs.lovable.dev/introduction/subscription-plans" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;plans&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://docs.lovable.dev/features/design-systems" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;design systems&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The two have converged: v0 imports existing repositories and opens pull requests, and its sandbox ships with Claude Code pre-installed in the terminal, on by default outside Enterprise and billed to the team's AI Gateway credits (&lt;a href="https://v0.app/docs/pre-installed-agents" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;v0 docs&lt;/a&gt;). What still separates them is the loop. v0's centers on the preview: prompt, look, adjust, publish. Claude Code's centers on the diff: prompt, read the change, run your type-check and tests, commit.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Who owns AI-generated UI code, and who maintains it?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You do: v0 and Lovable say so in their own terms, and Claude Code writes straight into your repository. The difference is where the source of truth lives and whether anything upstream can fix it later.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The v0 FAQ says "Vercel doesn't own the code generated based on your queries and prompts." Once you connect GitHub, the repository "becomes the source of truth for your project's code": each chat gets its own branch, v0 pushes changes to it automatically, and publishing merges a pull request. The Lovable FAQ says "Your apps, code, and the content you create with Lovable are yours." Claude Code edits your working tree, and you decide what gets committed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ownership has a second half the vendor FAQs skip: maintenance. Whatever generator writes them, generated screens have no upstream. When the sign-in screen mishandles a pasted one-time code, nobody ships a patch: you prompt for a fix, screen by screen, and hope each chat fixes it the same way.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Code installed from a registry has an upstream. Our blocks carry versions (in release 1.7.0 the Login Page is 1.0.1, the Pricing Page 1.1.0 and the Settings Page 1.0.0), the CLI records what it installed, and &lt;code&gt;update&lt;/code&gt; runs a 3-way merge that keeps your edits:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest outdated            &lt;span class="c"&gt;# installed items vs the latest release&lt;/span&gt;
npx wingo-ui@latest diff login-page     &lt;span class="c"&gt;# your file vs upstream&lt;/span&gt;
npx wingo-ui@latest update login-page   &lt;span class="c"&gt;# merge upstream changes into your edited file&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;That upstream comes with the code, whichever tool installs it; v0's agent also runs &lt;a href="https://v0.app/docs/agentic-features" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;shell commands in its sandbox&lt;/a&gt;, though we have not tried our CLI there. Our guide to &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/update-shadcn-components-without-losing-edits" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;updating copied components without losing edits&lt;/a&gt; shows the merge step by step.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How do you keep AI-built screens consistent?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Make every screen import the same component files, and give the agent rules that forbid anything else. "Match the other pages" in a prompt does not survive a new chat.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;v0's answer is Design Systems 2.0: you teach v0 your system once from an npm package, a repository or an app that uses it, and v0 saves it as a skill that a team owner on a paid plan can make the default for new chats. Its core rule is strict in the right way: "If a component, prop, or token cannot be verified from the sources, v0 should not use it." Two limits matter here: existing projects do not update when the skill changes (you ask v0 to update each one), and an import should stick to one design system and one framework stack where possible. Lovable copies a design system into &lt;code&gt;src/design-system/&amp;lt;slug&amp;gt;/&lt;/code&gt; of each connected project and offers new versions as an "Update available" prompt in the project chat.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With Claude Code, consistency lives in the repository. The three Wingo UI blocks share code at the file level: the Login Page, the Pricing Page and the Settings Page all import &lt;code&gt;Button&lt;/code&gt; from &lt;code&gt;@/components/ui/button&lt;/code&gt;, and their dependency trees share 13 registry items, among them the avatar, the toast, the spinner, the tones and the motion presets. Change the button file once and the sign-in submit, the plan buttons and the settings save bar change together.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every block also reads its defaults through the &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/ui-config" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;UI config&lt;/a&gt; provider, so one &lt;code&gt;UIProvider&lt;/code&gt; in the root layout sets the tone and corners of all three screens, and a prop on one page still wins:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/layout.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ReactNode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;UIProvider&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@/lib/ui-config&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;./globals.css&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// keyed by each block's data-slot name&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;defaults&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;login-page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;tone&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;brand&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;radius&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;lg&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;pricing-page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;tone&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;brand&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;ctaTone&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;brand&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;radius&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;lg&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;settings-page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;tone&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;brand&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;radius&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;lg&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;RootLayout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ReactNode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;lang&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"en"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;UIProvider&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;defaults&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;defaults&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;UIProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The rules file closes the loop: a few lines in &lt;code&gt;CLAUDE.md&lt;/code&gt; saying that screens are built from installed blocks and components and that the agent searches the MCP server before it writes UI. Our &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/claude-code-shadcn-mcp-setup" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Claude Code shadcn setup&lt;/a&gt; has the full block, and the &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/component-library-mcp-guide" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;component library MCP guide&lt;/a&gt; explains why the rules and the server need each other.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The sign-in screen below is the &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/login-page" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Login Page&lt;/a&gt; block with nothing wired; its simulated sign-in rejects passwords shorter than 8 characters.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Live demo: Login Page.&lt;/strong&gt; The original article embeds an interactive demo here (Sign in with a short password to see the error alert, then open Forgot password: the email you typed carries over). &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/v0-vs-claude-code-for-ui" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Try it live on wingo-ui.com&lt;/a&gt; or open the &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/login-page" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Login Page docs&lt;/a&gt;. Install: &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest add login-page&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How do you build sign-in, pricing and settings pages with Claude Code?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Install the blocks, then spend the agent on the wiring: handlers, data and routes, the part only your repository knows.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest login                                      &lt;span class="c"&gt;# Pro items need a signed-in key&lt;/span&gt;
npx wingo-ui@latest add login-page pricing-page settings-page
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The CLI writes the blocks to &lt;code&gt;components/blocks&lt;/code&gt;, everything they import to &lt;code&gt;components/ui&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;hooks&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;lib&lt;/code&gt;, and installs their npm packages. In release 1.7.0 the three blocks and their dependencies come to 83 registry items in 88 files. The blocks are Pro; the &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/button" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Button&lt;/a&gt; they share is free.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Each route is then one block with your handlers and copy. The sign-in page:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/(auth)/sign-in/page.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;use client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Link&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;next/link&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useRouter&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;next/navigation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;LoginPage&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@/components/blocks/login-page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;SignInRoute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;router&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useRouter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;LoginPage&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;layout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"centered"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;logo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"text-lg font-semibold"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Acme&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;labels&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;appName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Acme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;signInDescription&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Sign in to your Acme account to continue.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;methods&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;password&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;showProviders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;registerHref&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"/sign-up"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;linkComponent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Link&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onSignIn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;password&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;remember&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/api/auth/sign-in&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;POST&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;password&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;remember&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ok&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;The email or the password is not correct&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onSuccess&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;router&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;push&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/dashboard&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The pricing page, with your plans inside your own site header and footer:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/(marketing)/pricing/page.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;use client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Link&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;next/link&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useRouter&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;next/navigation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;PricingPage&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@/components/blocks/pricing-page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;PricingPlan&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@/components/ui/pricing-table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;PLANS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;PricingPlan&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;free&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Free&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;features&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;3 projects&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Community support&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;cta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Start for free&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;pro&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Pro&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;monthly&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;12&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;yearly&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;120&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;featured&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;features&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Unlimited projects&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Priority email support&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;cta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Start a 14 day trial&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;];&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;PricingRoute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;router&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useRouter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;PricingPage&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;plans&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;PLANS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;currencies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;labels&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Simple pricing for every team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;subtitle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Start free and upgrade when you need more projects.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;faqs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;question&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Can I cancel anytime?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;answer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Yes. Your plan stays active until the end of the period you paid for.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;header&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;footer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;showComparison&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;showLogos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;showTestimonials&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;showCta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;linkComponent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Link&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onSelectPlan&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;planId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;period&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;router&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;push&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`/checkout?plan=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;planId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;amp;period=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;period&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;On the &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/pricing-page" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Pricing Page&lt;/a&gt;, the period switch rolls every price to its new value, and in a column narrower than 768px, like the one below or a phone, the plans turn into a swipeable carousel that starts on the featured plan.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Live demo: Pricing Page.&lt;/strong&gt; The original article embeds an interactive demo here (Switch between Monthly and Yearly, then dollars and euros: every price rolls to its new value, and a plan's button spins before a toast confirms the choice). &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/v0-vs-claude-code-for-ui" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Try it live on wingo-ui.com&lt;/a&gt; or open the &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/pricing-page" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Pricing Page docs&lt;/a&gt;. Install: &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest add pricing-page&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And the settings page, saving each section to your API (password, two-step and session changes have their own handlers):&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/(app)/settings/page.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;use client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;SettingsPage&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@/components/blocks/settings-page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;SettingsRoute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;SettingsPage&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;sections&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;profil&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;cont&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;notificari&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;securitate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onSave&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;section&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;values&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`/api/settings/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;section&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;PUT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;values&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ok&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;We could not save. Please try again.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Three things the blocks leave to you:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Simulated handlers.&lt;/strong&gt; A handler you leave out stays simulated so the demo works: without &lt;code&gt;onVerifyCode&lt;/code&gt; the code views accept 123456, and without &lt;code&gt;onSave&lt;/code&gt; the settings page pretends to save.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Sample content.&lt;/strong&gt; The defaults describe demo companies: Northwind CRM on sign-in, Acme CRM on pricing, Emma Carter's profile in settings. Pass your own &lt;code&gt;labels&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;logo&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;plans&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;faqs&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;profile&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Section ids.&lt;/strong&gt; The settings sections are keyed by Romanian words (&lt;code&gt;profil&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;cont&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;notificari&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;facturare&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;securitate&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;pericol&lt;/code&gt;), while the labels default to English. The billing form validates a Romanian company ID (CUI) and a Romanian address, so leave &lt;code&gt;facturare&lt;/code&gt; out if you bill elsewhere.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A prompt that covers all three: "Build /sign-in, /pricing and /settings from the installed Wingo UI blocks, reading their props with get_block first. Wire every handler to app/api, list any on* handler left on its simulated default, then type-check and lint."&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/settings-page" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Settings Page&lt;/a&gt; below is narrower than 768px here, so it shows its phone layout: a list that pushes each section in.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Live demo: Settings Page.&lt;/strong&gt; The original article embeds an interactive demo here (Open Security and turn on two-step verification: copy the key, type 123456, then copy or download the ten backup codes). &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/v0-vs-claude-code-for-ui" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Try it live on wingo-ui.com&lt;/a&gt; or open the &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/settings-page" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Settings Page docs&lt;/a&gt;. Install: &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest add settings-page&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How much do v0, Lovable and Claude Code cost?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Entry plans cost about the same, $20 to $30 a month, but each meters something different: v0 pricing turns tokens into credits, Lovable charges credits per message, and Claude Code comes with a subscription's usage limits or bills API tokens. Prices as of October 2026, before tax:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Tool&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Free tier&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Paid plans&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What is metered&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://v0.app/pricing" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;v0&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;7 messages a day&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Plus $30 per user per month, with $30 of monthly credits and $2 of daily credits on login; Business $100 per user per month&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Tokens at per-model rates per million, for example $2 input and $10 output on v0 Pro, $5 and $25 on v0 Max&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://docs.lovable.dev/introduction/subscription-plans" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Lovable&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;5 build credits a day, up to 30 a month&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Pro $25 a month for 100 credits ($250 a year), with unlimited workspace members; Business $50 a month&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Credits per message, for example 0.50 for "Make the button gray" and 1.20 for "Add authentication with sign up and login"&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://claude.com/pricing" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Claude Code&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Not in Claude Free&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Claude Pro $20 a month or $17 billed yearly; Max from $100 a month; Team seats from $20 billed yearly&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Usage limits per plan, or API tokens with a Console key&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://cursor.com/pricing" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Cursor&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Hobby, limited agent requests&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Pro $20 a month; Teams $40 per user per month&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A set amount of model usage per plan, on-demand usage billed after&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/pricing" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Wingo UI&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;75 free items&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Pro $8 a month, $80 a year or $150 once&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Nothing; installing files uses no model tokens&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Lovable's credit examples come from its &lt;a href="https://lovable.dev/pricing" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;pricing page&lt;/a&gt;. We did not measure what each tool spends on these screens, so we put no price on a screen. One structural point is safe: the three blocks' own files are about 7,650 lines of TypeScript, and the settings page with its dependencies is 74 registry items. Generating screens of that depth costs output tokens or credits on every line, and again on every fix. Installing them costs none, and the agent's budget goes to the wiring.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


When should you use v0, and when Claude Code?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;v0 wins before there is a repository. Claude Code wins once there is one.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;v0 is the better choice when:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You need a clickable screen today, at a URL you can share. Deploys take one click.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A designer does the iterating. Design Mode edits styles visually on every plan, Free included, and on paid plans v0 &lt;a href="https://v0.app/docs/figma" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;turns a Figma link into a working app&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your stack is already Next.js, Tailwind CSS and shadcn/ui on Vercel, so v0's defaults are your defaults.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Claude Code is the better choice when:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The screens call your real APIs, with your environment variables, database and tests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are building the tenth screen of a product, and it has to match the first nine.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your stack is not v0's default: another framework, another component library, a monorepo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You want every change as a diff you read before it lands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Lovable vs Claude Code is a different question: who is building. Lovable suits a founder who does not want to read code and needs a hosted app with a database. It offers no framework choice and cannot connect an existing repository, so a developer with a Next.js codebase is better served by Claude Code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As of October 2026, a search for v0 vs Claude Code Reddit threads mostly returns comparison sites, and the advice they repeat is the hybrid: draft in v0, integrate with Claude Code. That holds, with one change for products with many screens: let the draft settle the layout, then build the real screens from components already in your repository, so the draft never becomes your design system.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Where does Cursor fit next to v0 and Claude Code?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In a v0 vs Cursor vs Claude Code comparison, Cursor sits on Claude Code's side of the line: an editor whose agent works on the files in your repository, and Claude Code runs inside it through the same extension it uses in VS Code (&lt;a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/overview" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Claude Code overview&lt;/a&gt;). Between those two, pick the interface you prefer; the v0 question stays the same.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Where should you start?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you have no repository yet and need something to show this week, start in v0 and connect GitHub from the first chat. If you have a repository, put the screens there. Connect the &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/docs/mcp" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Wingo UI MCP server&lt;/a&gt; with &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest agents install claude&lt;/code&gt;, install the three blocks and spend your prompts on wiring. The blocks are part of Wingo UI Pro; the Button they share and 74 other items are free.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Components in this post
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/login-page" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Login Page&lt;/a&gt; (Pro): The sign-in screen of Northwind CRM: password, email link or code, Google / Apple / Microsoft, two-step codes and the whole password recovery. Install: &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest add login-page&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/pricing-page" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Pricing Page&lt;/a&gt; (Pro): The pricing page of a SaaS: hero, plans with a monthly or yearly and dollar or euro switch, comparison, quotes, FAQ and a closing call. Install: &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest add pricing-page&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/settings-page" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Settings Page&lt;/a&gt; (Pro): The account settings of a back office: profile, account, notifications, billing, security and a danger zone, with a save bar. Install: &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest add settings-page&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


FAQ
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Is v0 better than Claude Code for building UI?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For a first draft you can click through and share, often yes: v0 shows a live preview, edits styles visually and deploys with one click. For screens that call your real API, follow your conventions and must match screens built months earlier, Claude Code fits better because it works in your repository with your files and rules.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Can I use v0 and Claude Code together?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yes. Connect the v0 project to GitHub and pull its branch into your local checkout for Claude Code. As of October 2026, v0 also pre-installs Claude Code in its sandbox terminal, where its requests use your team's AI Gateway credits.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Who owns the code that v0 or Lovable generates?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You do, by their own terms as of October 2026. The v0 FAQ says Vercel does not own the code generated from your prompts, and the Lovable FAQ says your apps, code and content are yours, subject to third-party rights such as open source licenses.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Does Lovable support Next.js?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No. As of October 2026 the Lovable FAQ says it does not offer a choice of framework: new apps use TanStack Start and older ones React with Vite. If your app runs on Next.js, v0 or Claude Code fit better.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


How much does Claude Code cost?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As of October 2026 it is not in Claude Free; it is included in Claude Pro at $20 a month, or $17 a month billed yearly, and in Max from $100 a month. It also runs on an Anthropic API key billed by usage, and Team seats start at $20 a month billed yearly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Can Claude Code install the Wingo UI login, pricing and settings pages?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yes. Run npx wingo-ui@latest add login-page pricing-page settings-page and the CLI writes the three blocks and everything they import into your project. They are Pro items, so sign in first with npx wingo-ui@latest login.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This article was originally published on the Wingo UI blog: &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/v0-vs-claude-code-for-ui" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;v0 vs Claude Code for UI: Ownership, Screens and Cost&lt;/a&gt;. The original has the live, interactive demos and is kept up to date.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Un formulario de registro puede parecer terminado cuando el usuario pulsa “Enviar”. En realidad, ahí empieza una parte delicada del producto: explicar si el correo se está enviando, si ya llegó, si caducó el enlace o si la persona debe intentarlo otra vez.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;En interfaces React es común resolverlo con un &lt;code&gt;isLoading&lt;/code&gt; y un mensaje verde para éxito. Funciona en una demo, pero se queda corto en producción. Un estado de email debe ser entendible sin color, anunciar sus cambios a un lector de pantalla y dejar una señal que el equipo pueda medir. La accesibilidad no es una capa final, es parte del contrato de la interfaz.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


El problema no es enviar el email, sino explicar su estado
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;La entrega de un mensaje tiene varios relojes: el navegador, la API, el proveedor de correo y la acción del usuario. Si la interfaz mezcla todos esos momentos, aparecen preguntas muy humanas: “¿debo hacer clic otra vez?”, “¿se perdió mi cuenta?” o “¿por que el botón sigue desactivado?”.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Un buen diseño separa al menos estas situaciones:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;idle&lt;/strong&gt;: todavía no se ha solicitado el mensaje.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;sending&lt;/strong&gt;: la aplicación recibió la acción y espera una respuesta.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;sent&lt;/strong&gt;: el backend aceptó la solicitud, pero eso no garantiza que el usuario ya lo leyó.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;verified&lt;/strong&gt;: el enlace fue confirmado correctamente.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;expired&lt;/strong&gt;: el enlace ya no es válido y se necesita uno nuevo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;error&lt;/strong&gt;: la aplicación no pudo completar o confirmar la operación.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Esta diferencia evita prometer “email entregado” cuando solo conocemos “solicitud aceptada”. También hace mas fácil diseñar copias, pruebas y métricas por separado.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Un modelo de estados pequeño y observable
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;En lugar de varios booleanos que pueden contradecirse, un estado discriminado mantiene una sola verdad visible:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;EmailState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;idle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;sending&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;sent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;expiresAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;verified&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;expired&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;El componente puede derivar de &lt;code&gt;kind&lt;/code&gt; el texto, el botón y el foco. El dato &lt;code&gt;expiresAt&lt;/code&gt; permite mostrar una fecha o un contador sin fingir que el mensaje seguirá siendo válido para siempre. Si el backend devuelve un identificador de intento, guardarlo como dato técnico ayuda a investigar reintentos duplicados.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Para flujos que necesitan contexto adicional, conviene estudiar patrones como las &lt;a href="https://dev.to/silviutech/llms-aprobaciones-por-email-con-contexto-minimo-jf1"&gt;aprobaciones por email con contexto mínimo&lt;/a&gt;. La idea útil aquí no es copiar el caso, sino mantener cada transición explicable.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


React y CSS para comunicar sin depender del color
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Un mensaje de éxito verde y un error rojo pueden ser una señal visual secundaria, nunca la única. El texto debe decir qué pasó y cuál es el siguiente paso. Por ejemplo, “Enlace enviado. Revisa tu bandeja y solicita otro en 45 segundos” es mucho mas accionable que “Listo”.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Para anunciar cambios dinámicos, un contenedor estable puede usar &lt;code&gt;role="status"&lt;/code&gt; para mensajes informativos y &lt;code&gt;role="alert"&lt;/code&gt; para errores que requieren atención inmediata. No conviene montar y desmontar varios anuncios a la vez: los lectores de pantalla pueden leerlos en un orden confuso.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;EmailNotice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;EmailState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;urgent&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;expired&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;copyFor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`email-notice email-notice--&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;urgent&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;alert&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;aria-live&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;urgent&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;assertive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;polite&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;En CSS, el estado debe conservar contraste, foco visible y una estructura legible con zoom. Un icono de reloj puede acompañar a &lt;code&gt;sending&lt;/code&gt;, pero el texto “Enviando…” sigue siendo necesario. Tambien es útil reservar una altura mínima para el aviso: así el formulario no salta cada vez que cambia el mensaje, algo pequeño que mejora la percepción de calidad.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Si el correo de prueba se consulta en un buzón aislado, un enlace como &lt;a href="https://dev.to/alexcarteruk/como-validar-correos-de-alertmanager-tras-rotar-secretos-en-kubernetes-4fi5"&gt;validar correos después de un cambio de infraestructura&lt;/a&gt; recuerda otra frontera importante: el frontend solo conoce la respuesta del flujo que está observando. Para una prueba manual, un &lt;a href="https://tempmailso.com" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;tp mail so&lt;/a&gt; puede servir para separar una dirección temporal del buzón personal; no debe usarse para datos sensibles ni confundirse con una confirmación de entrega.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Métricas y pruebas que respetan la accesibilidad
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Medir no significa registrar el contenido del mensaje ni la dirección completa. Es suficiente con eventos acotados, por ejemplo:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;email_verification_requested&lt;/code&gt; cuando el usuario inicia la solicitud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;email_verification_sent&lt;/code&gt; cuando la API acepta el envío.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;email_verification_resend&lt;/code&gt; cuando se pide otro enlace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;email_verification_verified&lt;/code&gt; cuando el token es válido.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;email_verification_expired&lt;/code&gt; cuando la persona vuelve tarde.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Con esos eventos se puede comparar la tasa de verificación, el tiempo hasta el éxito y la frecuencia de reenvíos. Un aumento de errores después de cambiar CSS no prueba una causa, pero sí indica dónde mirar. El dashboard debe evitar emails crudos; incluso un dato de prueba llamado “dummy e mail” merece el mismo cuidado que cualquier identificador.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Las pruebas frontend deberían cubrir teclado, foco, texto visible y anuncios. Un caso mínimo es: enviar, esperar el estado &lt;code&gt;sent&lt;/code&gt;, comprobar que el mensaje aparece una sola vez y verificar que el foco queda en un lugar razonable. Tambien hay que probar &lt;code&gt;expired&lt;/code&gt; y &lt;code&gt;error&lt;/code&gt; con mensajes largos, porque muchos diseños solo funcionan con una frase corta.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Preguntas frecuentes
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


¿&lt;code&gt;role="status"&lt;/code&gt; reemplaza al texto visible?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No. El rol ayuda a comunicar un cambio a tecnología asistiva, pero el mensaje visible sigue siendo necesario para personas que leen la pantalla sin usar un lector.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


¿Conviene usar un contador?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Sí, si explica una restricción real, como el tiempo antes de permitir otro envío. Debe actualizarse sin anunciar cada segundo, por que eso crea ruido. Anuncia el inicio y comunica cuando el botón vuelve a estar disponible.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


¿Debo decir “enviado” o “entregado”?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Di solo lo que el sistema puede demostrar. Si la API aceptó la solicitud, “solicitud enviada” o “revisa tu bandeja” es más preciso que “correo entregado”.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Checklist final
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[ ] Existe un estado explícito para cada resultado relevante.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[ ] El texto explica el siguiente paso sin depender del color.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[ ] Los avisos dinámicos tienen una estrategia de &lt;code&gt;aria-live&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[ ] El foco, el zoom y el teclado funcionan en éxito y error.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[ ] Las métricas no guardan el contenido ni la dirección completa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[ ] Se prueban reenvíos, expiración, latencia y mensajes largos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Un estado de email bien diseñado conecta React, CSS, accesibilidad y observabilidad. El resultado no es solo una pantalla mas bonita: es una interfaz que reduce dudas, evita reenvíos innecesarios y da al equipo señales claras para mejorarla.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every few months I end up needing a timeline in some app. A scheduling view, a project plan, a feed of events plotted against time. And every few months I rediscover that most timeline components fall apart once you give them real data. Fifty items, fine. A couple thousand? Scroll goes choppy, memory creeps up, and hovering over anything feels like wading through syrup.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The reason is usually the same. These libraries keep a DOM node for every single item. The browser is great at a lot of things, but keeping thousands of absolutely-positioned divs in sync while you pan around is not really one of them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://tempis.dev" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Tempis&lt;/a&gt; takes the other route and draws everything to a canvas. One element, no per-item nodes. So the question of "how many items can I show" stops being about your layout engine and starts being about how much you actually want on screen. It's held up fine for me past 5,000 items, and the whole thing is under 18 KB gzipped with zero dependencies, which I appreciated more than I expected to. Nothing else to audit, nothing else to break.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here's the smallest thing that does something useful:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;TempisTimeline&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@tempis/timeline&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;timeline&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;TempisTimeline&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;#canvas&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;responsive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Design&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span class="na"&gt;start&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;2026-01-05&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;2026-01-15&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;grouping&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Frontend&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Build&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;   &lt;span class="na"&gt;start&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;2026-01-12&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;2026-01-28&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;grouping&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Frontend&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Launch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span class="na"&gt;start&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;2026-01-30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;grouping&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Frontend&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;API&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;     &lt;span class="na"&gt;start&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;2026-01-08&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;2026-01-25&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;grouping&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Backend&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;range&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;start&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;2026-01-01&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;2026-02-01&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;position&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;bottom&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;An item with a &lt;code&gt;start&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;end&lt;/code&gt; is a range. An item with just a &lt;code&gt;start&lt;/code&gt; is a point in time. When they overlap, they stack themselves, so you're not doing lane-assignment math by hand. The &lt;code&gt;grouping&lt;/code&gt; field is what splits those four items into a Frontend row and a Backend row, and you can collapse groups, sort them your own way, and let people click a legend to filter by category. That legend-plus-grouping combo is the thing I reach for most, honestly. It turns a flat wall of bars into something you can actually read.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you're not on a build step, there's a CDN drop-in:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight html"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;script &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;src=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"https://unpkg.com/@tempis/timeline/dist/tempis_timeline.min.js"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/script&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;script&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;tempis_timeline&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;TempisTimeline&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;#canvas&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="cm"&gt;/* same options */&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/script&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Past the basics, the stuff that's saved me time: dependencies between items with the connector arrows routed automatically (and it doesn't fall over in RTL layouts), bands for drawing reference markers and lines across the whole thing, per-item styling when you need one bar to stand out, and animated &lt;code&gt;focus()&lt;/code&gt; to glide over to a specific item or date instead of teleporting. You can export the current view to a PNG if someone wants a screenshot for a deck. And if you've already standardized on Luxon or Day.js, there's a date adapter so you don't have to fight it over date handling.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The interactivity comes through callbacks, nothing exotic:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;TempisTimeline&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;#canvas&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onItemClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;openDetails&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onItemContextClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;pos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;showMenu&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;pos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onRangeChange&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;start&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetchVisibleData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;start&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;That last one is quietly the useful one. &lt;code&gt;onRangeChange&lt;/code&gt; fires as the visible window moves, so you can lazy-load and only pull the data that's actually in view instead of shipping everything up front. For a live feed or a big historical dataset that's the difference between snappy and not.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There's a React wrapper too, &lt;code&gt;@tempis/react&lt;/code&gt;, if you'd rather not manage the instance lifecycle yourself:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;TempisTimeline&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@tempis/react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;App&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;TempisTimeline&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;options&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;responsive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onItemClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;clicked&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;height&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;400&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;items&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;categories&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;bands&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;dependencies&lt;/code&gt; are props that sync on their own. When you need to do something imperative, like focus an item, grab the current range, or export an image, you reach for a ref:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ref&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;TempisTimelineRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ref&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;focus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;animate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;It's all TypeScript with real declarations, and the React package re-exports the core types so you're not installing two things just to import &lt;code&gt;TempisTimelineItem&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One bit of honesty before you &lt;code&gt;npm install&lt;/code&gt;: Tempis is source-available, not MIT. It's free for personal projects, learning, and evaluation, but commercial use that makes money needs a paid licence. Worth a look at the LICENSE so there are no surprises later.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you want to poke at it before writing any code, the &lt;a href="https://tempis.dev/examples.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;examples page&lt;/a&gt; has live demos, and the &lt;a href="https://tempis.dev/api/core/getting-started.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;getting started docs&lt;/a&gt; go deeper than this post does. If you end up building something with it, I'd genuinely like to hear what. The timeline UIs people come up with are always more interesting than the demos.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A while ago I wrote about why Google ignored my React SPA tool site and what I changed. I said I'd post an update and be straight about it if things didn't improve. So here it is: it worked for one page and did nothing for the two that matter most.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Some context: &lt;a href="https://pinfetcher.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;PinFetcher&lt;/a&gt; is an independent Pinterest downloader suite (not affiliated with Pinterest). I bought the domain as an expired one in August 2026, so it isn't a blank slate. A previous owner ran a WordPress site there, and Google still remembers some of those old URLs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What happened
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://pinfetcher.com/media-saver" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Media Saver&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, a page I added in October, was indexed within 2 days of my submitting it in URL Inspection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://pinfetcher.com/pinterest-video-downloader" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Pinterest Video Downloader&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and the &lt;a href="https://pinfetcher.com/pinterest-image-downloader" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;image downloader&lt;/a&gt;, my two core tools, still show &lt;code&gt;Last crawl: N/A&lt;/code&gt; in URL Inspection. That means Googlebot has not fetched them even once. I've requested indexing two or three times a month. Every time: "Indexing requested". Nothing changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What I verified on the stuck pages
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The same checklist as before:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The live test says "URL is available to Google".&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The rendered HTML has the full content (about 1,700 words), a self-referencing canonical, &lt;code&gt;index, follow&lt;/code&gt;, and no &lt;code&gt;noindex&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Both pages are in the sitemap and linked from the header on every page.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A quick way to check the raw HTML of any page:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;curl &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-s&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-o&lt;/span&gt; /dev/null &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-w&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"%{http_code}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; https://your-site.com/your-page
curl &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-s&lt;/span&gt; https://your-site.com/your-page | &lt;span class="nb"&gt;grep&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-oE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'&amp;lt;link rel="canonical"[^&amp;gt;]*&amp;gt;|&amp;lt;meta name="robots"[^&amp;gt;]*&amp;gt;'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


What Crawl Stats showed
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Google is visiting: 655 requests since Aug 5, so it isn't blocked.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;But 88% of them were "Refresh" (re-checking URLs it already knows) and only 12% were "Discovery". Google rarely finds new URLs on a young domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;38 requests were 404s on paths I never created (&lt;code&gt;/pl&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;/he&lt;/code&gt;, feed URLs). They're leftovers from the previous owner's site, and Google keeps rechecking them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The Links report gave me a lesson
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I had 8 external links from directories and profiles. &lt;strong&gt;All 8 point to the homepage.&lt;/strong&gt; None points to a tool page. I'd built a handful of listings, and every one sent trust to a single URL. If you want a specific page to be found, link to that page.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What I can't explain
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I don't know why Media Saver was fast and the older pages weren't. It's newer, I submitted it, and it has a lot of text, but I can't prove any of that was the reason, so I won't pretend I can.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What I'm doing now
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adding deep links to the two tool pages in my directory listings, my YouTube channel and this article.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;No more Request Indexing on those two pages. It hasn't helped.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Checking back in a week and posting the result either way.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Takeaways
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clean live test doesn't guarantee a crawl. It only rules out a bug on your side.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Check the Links report: do your external links point at the pages you want found?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Crawl Stats shows how much of Google's visiting is discovery. If it's mostly refresh, new URLs will wait.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If you bought an expired domain, expect old URLs to show up in your logs for months.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you've been through a "never crawled" phase on specific pages while others got indexed, what finally changed it for you?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As you keep building projects, you discover surprising challenges you didn't even know existed. Have you ever tried changing the style of a shadcn project from base UI to radix UI or vice versa?, it was an issue an encountered a while ago, and it can be a bit challenging to do as it isn't straight forward.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For a bit of context, I was building a project with other developers for a client, my work was to build like a sub-section of the website that still belongs to the main website. So I created a brand new React project, and set up shadcn to start building the website with pre-built UI components. Now one mistake I made was not considering the reusable components that were already created from the main project like the &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Header /&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Footer /&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, and so, I re-invented the wheel, creating those components again. This didn't look like an issue initially until a review was done, and the team noticed that the UI for the app I was building didn't match the UI of the main website.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After doing some checks in my project, I found out the issue was the type of style I was using when I installed shadcn. When you install shadcn, you would be asked to select the style you want to use (either base UI or radix UI). At first, I didn't think this really mattered, and honestly, it doesn't, but when you are working with other devs, it can be important to ensure your style matches what is being used. It can also matter if you want to get detailed about what it is you're trying to achieve, as different styles provide different ways of customizing your components from shadcn.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The main website uses the radix UI style, but my project was using base UI, and I had already built the entire UI using base UI, so I had to change it to radix UI. In other to change the style, here are the steps I took:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Step 1: Updating the 'style' property in my &lt;code&gt;components.json&lt;/code&gt; file
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/*
Each style in shadcn has variants (e,g vega, nova, maia etc)

You can discover the full list of variants each
style has from this page on shadcn's website — https://ui.shadcn.com/create

In my own case, the style was "base-nova", so I changed it to "radix-nova"
*/&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;style&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;radix-nova&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


Step 2: Reinstalled my components to ensure they match the new style
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After changing the style, I re-installed all the components I had installed previously in the &lt;code&gt;components/&lt;/code&gt; folder using this command:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;pnpm&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;dlx&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;add&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;shadcn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;@&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nd"&gt;latest&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;component&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// e.g. pnpm dlx add shadcn@latest button&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


Step 3: Updated my package.json file to reflect the style I am using
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I removed the base UI package, and replaced it with radix UI so as to ensure the components display properly. If you are changing from radix UI to base UI, the process is still the same&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;dependencies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@base-ui/react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;^1.7.0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Removed this&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;radix-ui&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;^1.4.3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Added this&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


Step 4: Update the node_modules folder
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Once I edited the package.json file, I ran &lt;code&gt;pnpm run update&lt;/code&gt; to update my node_modules folder, to install the radix UI package and remove base UI.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Conclusion
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With these steps, I was able to successfully change from base UI to radix UI, and if you follow the exact step, you can do the same as well. That was kind of simple right?, it isn't that hard once you know what to do, surprisingly, even the shadcn docs doesn't provide a tutorial on how to do this. Have you ever encountered this kind of issue of having to change the style of your shadcn project before?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A setting such as a booking link works on the server but shows up as &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; in the browser, with no error message and a passing build. In an AI-built (or hand-built) Next.js app, the usual causes are a variable name without the &lt;code&gt;NEXT_PUBLIC_&lt;/code&gt; prefix, or a variable added after the app was built.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We reproduced it on a small synthetic app, applied the smallest fix, and checked it by clicking the button in headless Chrome. Below: the symptom, the cause, the fix, how we verified it, and what we did &lt;strong&gt;not&lt;/strong&gt; test.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Short answer:&lt;/strong&gt; If a setting such as your booking link or API address works on the server but shows up as &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; in the browser, either the variable's name doesn't start with &lt;code&gt;NEXT_PUBLIC_&lt;/code&gt;, or you added it after the app was built. The smallest fix is to rename it (and the line of code that reads it) with the &lt;code&gt;NEXT_PUBLIC_&lt;/code&gt; prefix, then &lt;strong&gt;rebuild&lt;/strong&gt;. &lt;strong&gt;Verified on a synthetic app only.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Prerequisites
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Next.js app using the App Router (an &lt;code&gt;app/&lt;/code&gt; folder), with a setting stored as an environment variable (a &lt;code&gt;.env.local&lt;/code&gt; file or your host's "Environment Variables" page).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Terminal access, or your AI tool's code view and your host's settings page.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The symptom: a button, link or request in the browser uses the text &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; (for example a link that goes to &lt;code&gt;undefined/book&lt;/code&gt;). &lt;strong&gt;There is no error message, and the build passes.&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;No keys or accounts are needed for this fix.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Only rename settings that are safe for anyone to see.&lt;/strong&gt; A &lt;code&gt;NEXT_PUBLIC_&lt;/code&gt; value is copied into the code every visitor downloads. Secret keys (service-role keys, payment secrets, passwords) must never get this prefix. See "Security notes".&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The exact symptom
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There is no red error. This is what we saw in headless Chrome after clicking the button:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;text shown after clicking "Book a call": "undefined/book"
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The page's code was &lt;code&gt;process.env.BOOKING_URL + "/book"&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;BOOKING_URL=https://booking.example.test&lt;/code&gt; was set in &lt;code&gt;.env.local&lt;/code&gt;. The build log even says &lt;code&gt;Environments: .env.local&lt;/code&gt; and exits 0. If your code sends that value to a service, you will typically see failed requests or &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; inside a URL in your browser's Network tab instead (we did not test that part).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Versions we used
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Item&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Version&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Node.js&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;20.19.2&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;next&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;16.4.3 (Turbopack)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;react / react-dom&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;19.3.1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Browser&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Google Chrome 155.0.8059.84, headless, via playwright-core 1.64.1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;OS&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Linux, single machine&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Cause
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Next.js runs your code in two places: on the server, and in your visitor's browser. The browser can't see your server's settings. To let it see a setting, Next.js copies the value into the downloaded JavaScript when you run &lt;code&gt;next build&lt;/code&gt;, but &lt;strong&gt;only&lt;/strong&gt; for variables whose names start with &lt;code&gt;NEXT_PUBLIC_&lt;/code&gt;, and only if the variable exists at that moment (&lt;a href="https://nextjs.org/docs/app/guides/environment-variables" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;official docs&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That gives two common ways to get &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;No prefix.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;BOOKING_URL&lt;/code&gt; stays on the server. In the browser, &lt;code&gt;process.env.BOOKING_URL&lt;/code&gt; is empty. In our built bundle the code was still a lookup at click time: &lt;code&gt;process.env.BOOKING_URL+"/book"&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Added too late.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;NEXT_PUBLIC_BOOKING_URL&lt;/code&gt; is right, but it wasn't set when &lt;code&gt;next build&lt;/code&gt; ran (for example you added it to your host's settings after the last deploy). The value is "frozen" at build time, so the browser still gets &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; until you rebuild. We reproduced this too: building with no variable, then adding &lt;code&gt;.env.local&lt;/code&gt; and restarting &lt;code&gt;next start&lt;/code&gt; still gave &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Public reports of the same family: the &lt;a href="https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/74624" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Next.js discussion #74624&lt;/a&gt; (Next 15 + React 19 + Turbopack) and a &lt;a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/68205264/environment-variables-in-nextjs-are-undefined" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Stack Overflow answer&lt;/a&gt; saying env files are read when the server starts and production needs a rebuild. We found these through web search and did not measure how common the problem is, or how often AI tools cause it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Smallest working fix
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rename the variable everywhere it is set (&lt;code&gt;.env.local&lt;/code&gt; and your host's settings) from &lt;code&gt;BOOKING_URL&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;NEXT_PUBLIC_BOOKING_URL&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Change the code that reads it to the same name, written exactly as &lt;code&gt;process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_BOOKING_URL&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rebuild and redeploy (locally: stop the server, run &lt;code&gt;npx next build&lt;/code&gt;, start again; in dev, stop and restart &lt;code&gt;npm run dev&lt;/code&gt;). On a host, trigger a new deploy after saving the variable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Before (shows &lt;code&gt;undefined/book&lt;/code&gt;): &lt;code&gt;app/BookButton.js&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;use client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;BookButton&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;link&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setLink&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setLink&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;BOOKING_URL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/book&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Book&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;call&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;link&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;link&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;.env.local&lt;/code&gt;: &lt;code&gt;BOOKING_URL=https://booking.example.test&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


After (shows the real link)
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="gd"&gt;-      &amp;lt;button onClick={() =&amp;gt; setLink(process.env.BOOKING_URL + "/book")}&amp;gt;Book a call&amp;lt;/button&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+      &amp;lt;button onClick={() =&amp;gt; setLink(process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_BOOKING_URL + "/book")}&amp;gt;Book a call&amp;lt;/button&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;.env.local&lt;/code&gt;: &lt;code&gt;NEXT_PUBLIC_BOOKING_URL=https://booking.example.test&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Write it exactly as &lt;code&gt;process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_NAME&lt;/code&gt;. Per the Next.js docs and the discussion linked above, forms like &lt;code&gt;process.env[name]&lt;/code&gt;, saving &lt;code&gt;process.env&lt;/code&gt; in a variable first, or optional chaining (&lt;code&gt;process?.env?.NAME&lt;/code&gt;) are not replaced. &lt;strong&gt;We did not test those forms.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If the value must be changeable without rebuilding, or must stay secret, don't use &lt;code&gt;NEXT_PUBLIC_&lt;/code&gt;. Read the value in server code and give the browser only what it needs, for example through your own API route. &lt;strong&gt;We did not test that approach.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Copyable prompt for your AI coding tool
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;In my Next.js App Router app, a setting works on the server but is undefined in the browser. Find every place in files marked "use client" (or components imported by them) that reads process.env.SOMETHING where SOMETHING does not start with NEXT_PUBLIC_. For each one, tell me whether the value is safe for any visitor to see. For the safe ones only, rename the variable to NEXT_PUBLIC_SOMETHING in the code, in .env.local and in .env.example, and write the access exactly as process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SOMETHING (no optional chaining, no process.env[name], no aliasing). For secrets (keys, tokens, passwords), do NOT add the prefix; instead move that code to a server route and tell me. Do not change anything else, show me the diff, and remind me to set the renamed variables on my host and redeploy.
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Review the diff yourself and check no secret got the prefix. We did not test this prompt in any AI tool.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How we verified
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Run on 2026-10-24 on a small synthetic app (three copies: before, after, and "added too late"), using headless Chrome with default settings.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Builds pass either way:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;next build&lt;/code&gt; exited 0 for before and after. The build does not catch this.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Before, production (&lt;code&gt;next build&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;next start&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/strong&gt; after the click the page showed &lt;code&gt;undefined/book&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Before, dev (&lt;code&gt;next dev&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/strong&gt; same result, &lt;code&gt;undefined/book&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;After, production and dev:&lt;/strong&gt; the page showed &lt;code&gt;https://booking.example.test/book&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Bundle check:&lt;/strong&gt; the built "before" code still reads &lt;code&gt;process.env.BOOKING_URL&lt;/code&gt; at click time, while the "after" code has the link written into it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Added-too-late case (correctly named variable):&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;built with no &lt;code&gt;.env.local&lt;/code&gt;, then started: &lt;code&gt;undefined/book&lt;/code&gt;;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;then added &lt;code&gt;.env.local&lt;/code&gt; and restarted the server without rebuilding: still &lt;code&gt;undefined/book&lt;/code&gt;;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;then rebuilt and restarted: &lt;code&gt;https://booking.example.test/book&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every run also logged one unrelated &lt;code&gt;404&lt;/code&gt; resource error that we did not identify (probably a missing icon file); we did not confirm which file it was.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Not verified
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other browsers (Firefox, Safari) and real phones or visitors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other Next.js, React or Node versions, and the Pages Router.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vercel, Netlify, Cloudflare, Lovable, Bolt or other hosts: where and when they apply variables during their build. We only simulated "variable missing at build time" locally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vite-style apps (&lt;code&gt;VITE_&lt;/code&gt; names and &lt;code&gt;import.meta.env&lt;/code&gt;). A &lt;a href="https://docs.nextlovable.com/cli/what-breaks" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;third-party migration guide&lt;/a&gt; says exported Lovable apps need &lt;code&gt;VITE_&lt;/code&gt; renamed to &lt;code&gt;NEXT_PUBLIC_&lt;/code&gt;; we did not test that.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The optional-chaining, &lt;code&gt;process.env[name]&lt;/code&gt; and aliasing cases, and the "read it on the server and pass it down" alternative.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;What a real service request does when given an &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; URL; we only checked the text the page built.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Code generated by Cursor, Lovable, Bolt or v0; our app is hand-written and synthetic. We did not measure how often AI tools produce an unprefixed name.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Whether the AI prompt produces a correct and safe diff in any tool.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Troubleshooting
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Still &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; after renaming:&lt;/strong&gt; you probably didn't rebuild. Stop the server, rebuild, start again; on a host, redeploy after saving the variable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Works in &lt;code&gt;npm run dev&lt;/code&gt; but not on your live site:&lt;/strong&gt; the host's build may not have the variable. Add it in the host's settings under the exact same name, then redeploy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Check that &lt;code&gt;.env.local&lt;/code&gt; is in the project root&lt;/strong&gt; (the folder with &lt;code&gt;package.json&lt;/code&gt;) and the name has no typos or spaces around &lt;code&gt;=&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Mixed up the two places:&lt;/strong&gt; a variable set only on your laptop isn't on your host, and vice versa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Security notes
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anything named &lt;code&gt;NEXT_PUBLIC_&lt;/code&gt; ends up in the code anyone can download and read. Use it only for values meant to be public (a booking link, a public analytics ID, a publishable key). Never for a service-role key, secret key, password or token.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Never paste real keys into an AI chat; use placeholders like &lt;code&gt;https://booking.example.test&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Don't commit &lt;code&gt;.env.local&lt;/code&gt; to a public repository.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;p&gt;The original guide, with the before/after files, is on The Agent Ledger: &lt;a href="https://theagentledger.ai/fixes/next-public-env-undefined-in-browser/?utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_medium=post&amp;amp;utm_campaign=fix04" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;A setting shows as "undefined" in the browser: Next.js fix&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;AI disclosure: This article was written with the help of AI. The reproduction and the before/after browser runs described above were actually performed and checked against the logs before publishing.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You need to let users pay with Stripe in your Next.js app, but you're not sure how to create the checkout flow, keep your DB in sync, and give customers a self-service portal.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 1: Create the Stripe account and products
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sign up at &lt;a href="https://stripe.com" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://stripe.com&lt;/a&gt; and stay in test mode.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Products &amp;gt; Add product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Name: "Pro Plan"&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pricing: Recurring, $29/month (add an annual price at $290/year for the discount)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Save and copy the price ID (&lt;code&gt;price_xxx&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Repeat for each tier (Starter, Pro, Enterprise). Grab two keys from the dashboard:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;pk_test_...&lt;/code&gt; in test mode)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;STRIPE_SECRET_KEY&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;sk_test_...&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You'll also need a webhook signing secret later.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 2: Install the SDK
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npm &lt;span class="nb"&gt;install &lt;/span&gt;stripe @stripe/stripe-js
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Add the keys to &lt;code&gt;.env.local&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;pk_test_...
&lt;span class="nv"&gt;STRIPE_SECRET_KEY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;sk_test_...
&lt;span class="nv"&gt;STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;whsec_...
&lt;span class="nv"&gt;NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;http://localhost:3000
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Create a Stripe client wrapper at &lt;code&gt;lib/stripe.ts&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Stripe&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;stripe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;stripe&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Stripe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;STRIPE_SECRET_KEY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;apiVersion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;2025-10-29.acacia&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;typescript&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


Step 3: Build the Checkout Session
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Create a server action to start checkout:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;use server&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;stripe&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@/lib/stripe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;auth&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@clerk/nextjs/server&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;redirect&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;next/navigation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createCheckoutSession&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;priceId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;auth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Unauthorized&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;stripe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;checkout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;sessions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;create&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;mode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;subscription&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;line_items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;priceId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;quantity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;success_url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/billing/success?session_id={CHECKOUT_SESSION_ID}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;cancel_url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/billing`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;client_reference_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;metadata&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;subscription_data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;metadata&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;allow_promotion_codes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;automatic_tax&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;enabled&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;redirect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Key points:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;client_reference_id&lt;/code&gt; links the session to your user.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;metadata&lt;/code&gt; on the session and subscription gives redundant traceability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;allow_promotion_codes&lt;/code&gt; enables discount codes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;automatic_tax&lt;/code&gt; turns on Stripe Tax (requires setup).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 4: Trigger Checkout from the UI
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;use client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;createCheckoutSession&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@/app/actions/stripe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;CheckoutButton&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;priceId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;priceId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;form&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;action&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createCheckoutSession&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;priceId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"submit"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;form&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;When the button is clicked, the server action creates a session and redirects the user to Stripe-hosted checkout. After payment they return to &lt;code&gt;/billing/success&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 5: Wire the Webhook
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Stripe updates its own records; without a webhook your DB never knows a payment succeeded.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Create &lt;code&gt;app/api/webhooks/stripe/route.ts&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;next/headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;stripe&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@/lib/stripe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@/lib/db&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Stripe&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;stripe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;POST&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;req&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;req&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;signature&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;stripe-signature&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;signature&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Missing signature&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;400&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Stripe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;stripe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;webhooks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;constructEvent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;signature&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;catch &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`Webhook signature failed: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;400&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;switch &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;case&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;checkout.session.completed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;object&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;client_reference_id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;metadata&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;subscription&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;subscription&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;upsert&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;create&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;stripeCustomerId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;customer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;as &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;stripeSubscriptionId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;subscription&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;as &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;active&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;stripeCustomerId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;customer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;as &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;stripeSubscriptionId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;subscription&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;as &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;active&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;break&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;case&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;customer.subscription.updated&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sub&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;object&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;subscription&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;stripeSubscriptionId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;currentPeriodEnd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;sub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current_period_end&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;cancelAtPeriodEnd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;cancel_at_period_end&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;break&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;case&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;customer.subscription.deleted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sub&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;object&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;subscription&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;stripeSubscriptionId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;canceled&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;break&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;case&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;invoice.payment_failed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;invoice&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;object&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Notify the user, mark subscription as past_due, etc.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;break&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;OK&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;In the Stripe dashboard, add a webhook endpoint pointing to &lt;code&gt;https://your-app.com/api/webhooks/stripe&lt;/code&gt; and subscribe to:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;checkout.session.completed&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;customer.subscription.updated&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;customer.subscription.deleted&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;invoice.payment_failed&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;invoice.paid&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Copy the webhook signing secret (&lt;code&gt;whsec_...&lt;/code&gt;) into &lt;code&gt;STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For local development, forward events with the Stripe CLI:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;stripe listen &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--forward-to&lt;/span&gt; http://localhost:3000/api/webhooks/stripe
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The CLI prints a local &lt;code&gt;whsec_...&lt;/code&gt; secret you can use during dev.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 6: Stripe Customer Portal
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Instead of building your own subscription management UI, redirect users to Stripe's portal.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;use server&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;stripe&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@/lib/stripe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;auth&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@clerk/nextjs/server&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@/lib/db&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;redirect&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;next/navigation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;openCustomerPortal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;auth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Unauthorized&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;subscription&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;subscription&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;findUnique&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;subscription&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;No subscription&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;stripe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;billingPortal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;sessions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;create&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;customer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;subscription&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;stripeCustomerId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;return_url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/billing`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;redirect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The portal lets users upgrade/downgrade plans, update payment methods, download invoices, and cancel. Enable the desired features in Stripe under Settings &amp;gt; Customer portal.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 7: Enable Stripe Tax (optional)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you need to collect sales tax, enable Stripe Tax in the dashboard (Settings &amp;gt; Tax). Register the jurisdictions where you have nexus and assign tax codes to your prices. With &lt;code&gt;automatic_tax: { enabled: true }&lt;/code&gt; in the checkout session, Stripe will calculate and collect tax automatically.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You can skip this step for a US-only, pre-revenue product and add it later when you cross a state's economic nexus threshold.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Step 8: One-Time Payments (non-subscription)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For a single purchase, set &lt;code&gt;mode: 'payment'&lt;/code&gt; instead of &lt;code&gt;'subscription'&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;stripe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;checkout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;sessions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;create&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;mode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;payment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;line_items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;priceId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;quantity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;success_url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/checkout/success`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;cancel_url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/checkout`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;client_reference_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;metadata&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;one_time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The same webhook (&lt;code&gt;checkout.session.completed&lt;/code&gt;) fires; grant lifetime access in your DB rather than creating a subscription record.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Common Gotchas
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Skipping webhooks entirely.&lt;/strong&gt; Users can pay, Stripe shows a successful charge, but your app never records it. Implement the webhook before you go live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Mismatched environment keys.&lt;/strong&gt; Using a live publishable key with a test secret (or vice-versa) causes "Invalid API Key" errors. Keep test and production keys separate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Forgot to set &lt;code&gt;client_reference_id&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; Without it you can't reliably map a checkout session back to your user in the webhook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Webhook URL not reachable.&lt;/strong&gt; In production the endpoint must be publicly accessible and use HTTPS; otherwise Stripe will keep retrying and eventually disable the webhook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Tax settings not enabled but &lt;code&gt;automatic_tax&lt;/code&gt; set.&lt;/strong&gt; Stripe will reject the session creation; either enable Stripe Tax or remove the flag.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Address these issues early and the Stripe integration will stay in sync with your Next.js app.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is a shorter version of a guide I wrote on thefrontkit. The &lt;a href="https://thefrontkit.com/blogs/add-stripe-payments-to-nextjs-template-2026?utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_medium=syndication" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;full post&lt;/a&gt; has the complete walkthrough.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I used to paste “make this component accessible” into ChatGPT and hope for the best. Sometimes I got a &lt;code&gt;role="button"&lt;/code&gt; on a real &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;button&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. Sometimes the contrast “fix” was &lt;code&gt;#666&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;#fff&lt;/code&gt; with no math behind it. The model wasn’t dumb — my prompt was.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Once I stopped asking for vibes and started asking for a checklist the model had to fill, the diffs got usable. Here’s the prompt shape I use for React UI, and why each bucket matters.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Soft prompts produce soft a11y
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Vague asks produce vague markup:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;“Make it accessible” → random &lt;code&gt;aria-label&lt;/code&gt;s, duplicate roles, no keyboard path&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;“Add ARIA” → decorative icons announced twice, interactive divs with no Enter/Space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;“Fix contrast” → a hex that &lt;em&gt;looks&lt;/em&gt; darker, not one that passes 4.5:1&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You’re outsourcing judgment without giving constraints. Models are great at filling a schema. They’re mediocre at inventing your team’s a11y bar from a one-liner.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The three buckets I always force
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I put every generation (or agent edit) through the same three headings. If any heading is empty in the reply, I reject the draft.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


1. Roles (and native elements first)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ask the model to prefer HTML semantics, then ARIA only when needed:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;For each interactive or landmark node in the component:
- Prefer a native element (&amp;lt;button&amp;gt;, &amp;lt;a href&amp;gt;, &amp;lt;input&amp;gt;, &amp;lt;nav&amp;gt;, &amp;lt;main&amp;gt;).
- If you use a custom role, name the role and the reason native HTML wasn’t enough.
- Never put role="button" on a &amp;lt;button&amp;gt;.
- List every aria-* you add and what user need it covers.
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;That last line kills cargo-cult attributes. If the model can’t say &lt;em&gt;why&lt;/em&gt; &lt;code&gt;aria-describedby&lt;/code&gt; exists, it shouldn’t invent it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


2. Keyboard
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Sighted mouse testing lies. Force an explicit path:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Describe the keyboard path for this UI:
- Tab order (which nodes are focusable, in what order)
- Activation keys (Enter / Space for buttons; arrows only if you implement a composite widget)
- Escape / dismiss behavior for overlays
- Focus return target after close
- Visible focus styles (class or CSS custom property — don’t rely on outline: none alone)
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;If the answer is “user can click,” the prompt failed. Composite widgets (menus, tabs, listboxes) need more than Tab — but most “buttons” and “links” don’t need arrow-key theater. Make the model justify complexity.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


3. Contrast
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Don’t accept “looks fine.” Ask for numbers:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;For text and UI chrome in this component:
- Foreground / background pairs (hex or token names)
- Target ratio: 4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text and non-text UI (WCAG 2.x AA)
- Show the calculated ratio or admit you didn’t calculate it
- If using design tokens, name the token — don’t invent a one-off hex
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Models will still approximate ratios. That’s fine — the point is they have to &lt;em&gt;show&lt;/em&gt; the pair. Reviewers catch math errors faster than they catch “I made it darker.”&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


A full prompt template I actually paste
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;You are editing a React + TypeScript component. Return:
1) the full updated component
2) a short a11y report with three sections: Roles, Keyboard, Contrast

Rules:
- Native elements before ARIA
- No role on elements that already have that implicit role
- Keyboard path must be documented; no mouse-only flows
- Contrast: list fg/bg pairs and target ratios (AA)
- Do not add product marketing or unrelated refactors
- Keep existing design tokens; don’t invent new color literals unless necessary

Component / context:
&amp;lt;paste code or file path summary&amp;gt;

User story:
&amp;lt;e.g. “Filter chips in a toolbar; one chip can be selected; Clear resets”&amp;gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The user story matters. Without it, the model guesses wrong focus order (e.g. putting “Clear” before the chips because it appeared first in the JSX).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What I reject on sight
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Even with a structured prompt, I still throw away drafts that:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wrap everything in &lt;code&gt;div&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;role&lt;/code&gt; when a &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;button&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; would do&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set &lt;code&gt;tabIndex={0}&lt;/code&gt; on static text “for accessibility”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use &lt;code&gt;aria-label&lt;/code&gt; that duplicates visible text (screen readers hear it twice in some setups)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remove focus outlines without a replacement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Claim “WCAG AAA” with no pairs listed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Structured prompts don’t replace review. They make review cheaper.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Wiring this into an agent loop
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you use Copilot Chat, Cursor, or a custom agent on PRs:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Put the three-bucket checklist in the system or project prompt (once).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ask the agent to fail the turn if any bucket is missing — same as a CI check.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep a golden example: one good Button, one good Modal, one good Combobox. Point the model at those files instead of the open web.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I keep the checklist in the repo (&lt;code&gt;docs/a11y-prompt.md&lt;/code&gt;) so humans and agents share one source. When WCAG guidance or our token names change, we edit that file — not twelve ChatGPT threads.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Tiny example: what changes in the output
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Soft prompt:&lt;/strong&gt; “Make this accessible.”&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You get a &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;div onClick&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;role="button"&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;aria-label="Submit"&lt;/code&gt;, no keyboard handler, contrast unchecked.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Structured prompt:&lt;/strong&gt; same UI, three buckets required.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You get a &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;button type="submit"&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, focus ring via existing &lt;code&gt;--focus-ring&lt;/code&gt; token, Enter/Space free because it’s a real button, and a report line: &lt;code&gt;text/primary on surface/default ≈ 7.2:1&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Same model. Different ask.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Start tonight
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You don’t need a new tooling stack. Copy the three buckets into your next AI edit. Reject incomplete reports. After a week you’ll notice fewer “a11y polish” follow-up PRs — not because the model got smarter, but because you stopped asking it to invent the rubric.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If your team already has an a11y lint (eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y, axe in CI), keep it. Structured prompts catch the design intent those linters never see: focus return, composite widget behavior, and whether that new hex belongs in the token set at all.&lt;/p&gt;
